    "title": "TSA employees at Texarkana Regional work without pay during government shutdown - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Fred Gamble ,\n6 hours ago TEXARKANA, Ark. (KSLA) - Airline passengers are arriving hours early for flights as TSA employees continue to work without pay amid the partial government shutdown. Texarkana Regional Airport, which has 13 TSA employees on staff, is among the airports feeling the effects — those workers received no pay in their most recent paychecks. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
